  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 103.29 Incinerator",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 103.29 “Incinerator” means “incinerator” as defined in RSA 149-M:4, X-a, namely “a facility which employs a method of using controlled thermal combustion, including flame combustion, to thermally break down waste or other materials, including refuse-derived fuel, to an ash residue that contains little or no combustible materials.”\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100) #8460-B, eff 10-28-05; ss by #14103, effective 10-23-24 (formerly Env-Sw 103.25) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
